plymouth-theme-debian-slider (1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop the frames of the old two-step version from theme/images: the script
    never loaded them, but they made up 95 % of the images, went into the
    initramfs and failed make check, which broke the package build.
  * Install only the images the script loads.
  * Cut status lines and typed text that do not fit with an ellipsis, on
    UTF-8 character boundaries.
  * hide-message hides only the message it names.
  * Snap the scale down, so the splash stays within its share of the screen.
  * Lower the refresh rate to 60 Hz.
  * Ask for the generic Sans font, the one Debian's initramfs hook ships.

 -- nuxster <nuxster@gmail.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300

plymouth-theme-debian-slider (1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Switch from the two-step module to the script module and scale the splash
    to 30 % of the screen height, so it looks the same at every resolution.
  * Ship the images in 1x and 2x sets rendered from src/logo.svg.
  * Drop the outdated keymap-render.png, which no longer matched plymouth's
    keymap table and showed the wrong layout name in the password dialog.
  * Show a progress bar with a title while installing updates.
  * Fill the bar left to right at the end of the boot, triggered by
    systemd-user-sessions.service: the script module's quit function runs
    after plymouth has stopped drawing, and GDM and LightDM deactivate
    plymouth as soon as they start, so the highlight used to freeze
    mid-slide for the last seconds of the boot.

 -- nuxster <nuxster@gmail.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300

plymouth-theme-debian-slider (1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging.
  * Add tools/render.py to regenerate the frames from src/logo.png.
  * Keep Debian's injected watermark.png wordmark at the bottom edge.

 -- nuxster <nuxster@gmail.com>  Thu, 18 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
